      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Letting the shell rest\" means giving yourself permission to stop fighting the void for a while. You don't have to build anything new when the foundation feels like dust; just let the exhaustion settle in. That emptiness you feel isn't a failure, it's the space where the pain is living, and sometimes the only honest thing to do is just let it be there. There's no point in forcing yourself to be something you're not right now.",
